{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are implementing GitHub issue #9 in user/delegate: gate, change-set, idle watchdog, and a cross-process write lock for the `delegate` CLI. Do not delegate further: no subagents, no cursor_run, no delegate tools. Follow the repo's AGENTS.md.\n\nRead first: `gh issue view 9`, the owner rulings in `gh issue view 9 --comments` and `gh issue view 7 --comments`, spec `gh issue view 4` (Job model, Status record, Write lock). Then src/cli.rs, src/status_record.rs, src/finalize.rs, src/gate.rs, src/git.rs, tests/cli_e2e.rs.\n\nWorking directory: this worktree, branch `9-gate-lock`. Stay on it; do not create branches. Commit when done; do not push.\n\n## What already exists (reuse it, don't rebuild it)\nThe supervisor (`supervise` in src/cli.rs) drives one job through `JobRegistry`, which already runs the gate (finalize.rs `run_gate_ctx` → gate.rs), computes the git change-set and the \"commits landed but tree still dirty\" concern (finalize.rs), and runs the idle watchdog (model-idle / tool-idle windows, STALLED on kill). #9 is mostly wiring plus the file lock:\n\n1. `run` accepts `--gate CMD` and `--tool-idle-ms N`; pass both to the supervisor and into `JobSpec` (`gate`, `tool_idle_ms`) and `ResumeContext.gate`. Store `gate` and `toolIdleMs` in the record's `resume` object (CliResume) so #10 can resume with them.\n2. Gate timeout (ruling 2): the gate is killed after the job's tool-idle window (spec.tool_idle_ms, else the deps default 1800000). Add a `gate_timeout_ms` to `FinalizeCtx` and pass it to `GateOpts.timeout_ms`.\n3. Change-set (ruling 5): read-write CLI jobs always report `changeSet` with new commits; the dirty-tree concern stays on (no allow-partial-commit flag in the CLI).\n4. Watchdog: idle defaults 300000 / 1800000 already come from the host profile; just thread `--tool-idle-ms`. For tests, `DELEGATE_IDLE_MS` env (like the existing `DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS`) may override the model-idle window in the supervisor. A STALLED record must say why (the existing finalize text).\n5. Write lock (rulings 1, 3, 7): new src/lock.rs. Read-only jobs take no lock. For read-write, `run` opens `$TMPDIR/delegate-locks/<hex hash of canonical cwd>.lock` and takes `flock(LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB)` BEFORE spawning the supervisor. On EWOULDBLOCK it reads the holder job id from the file, prints `BUSY <holderJobId>` to stderr, exits 3. On success it truncates the file, writes its own job id, and lets the supervisor inherit the locked fd (clear FD_CLOEXEC; pass the fd number as a supervisor arg). The kernel releases the lock when the supervisor exits or dies, so nothing has to clean up. `libc` is already a dependency. Use `std::hash::DefaultHasher` or similar for the hash; no new crates.\n6. Dead supervisor (ruling 7, deferred from #7): `watch` treats a RUNNING record whose `supervisorPid` is no longer alive (`kill(pid, 0)` fails with ESRCH) as terminal: rewrite the record as status `ERROR` with text \"supervisor died\" and print it. Keep it to that.\n\n## Literal examples\nBUSY stderr line:\n```\nBUSY 5b0a1c52-3f0e-4c8e-9a51-2f7d0c1e9b44\n```\nTerminal record (one line in `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/<id>.json`; pretty-printed here):\n```\n{\"status\":\"DONE_WITH_CONCERNS\",\"result\":{\"status\":\"DONE_WITH_CONCERNS\",\"text\":\"Fixed add().\\nSTATUS: DONE\",\"sessionId\":\"s-1\",\"backend\":\"cursor\",\"model\":\"composer-2.5\",\"usage\":null,\"costUsd\":null,\"costEstimated\":false,\"durationMs\":812,\"jobId\":\"5b0a1c52-3f0e-4c8e-9a51-2f7d0c1e9b44\",\"gateResult\":{\"command\":\"python3 test_calc.py\",\"exitCode\":1,\"passed\":false,\"outputTail\":\"AssertionError\"},\"changeSet\":{\"headBefore\":\"8edd623\",\"headAfter\":\"e31bb77\",\"newCommits\":[\"e31bb77 Fix add\"],\"filesChanged\":[\"calc.py\"],\"diffstat\":\" calc.py | 2 +-\",\"uncommittedFiles\":[],\"dirtyAfter\":false}},\"supervisorPid\":4242,\"lastHeartbeatAt\":1790840779963,\"resume\":{\"model\":\"composer-2.5\",\"cwd\":\"/tmp/w\",\"capability\":\"read-write\",\"sessionId\":\"s-1\",\"gate\":\"python3 test_calc.py\",\"toolIdleMs\":null}}\n```\nCheck field names against the real serializer (types.rs RunOutput/GateResult/ChangeSet, status_record.rs CliRecord) and follow the code where this example differs.\n\n## File fence\nOwns: src/cli.rs (run/supervise/watch paths; do not add subcommands), src/lock.rs (new), src/lib.rs (module line), src/status_record.rs, src/finalize.rs, src/gate.rs, src/git.rs, tests/cli_e2e.rs, and in src/job_registry.rs ONLY the `FinalizeCtx { .. }` construction (gate timeout). Forbidden: config/, src/models.rs, src/config.rs, src/doctor*.rs, src/index*, other parts of src/job_registry*, src/tool_schemas.rs, .github/. A parallel lane adds `models`/`doctor` arms to src/cli.rs's dispatch match; don't touch that match beyond what you need. Need anything else? Stop and report instead.\n\n## Tests (TDD against the e2e seam in tests/cli_e2e.rs; drive the real binary)\nCover: gate pass (DONE kept, gateResult.passed true); gate fail (DONE → DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, output recorded); change-set lists a commit the fake agent made; dirty-after-commit concern; silent fake agent STALLED after a tiny idle window with the reason in the record; second read-write run in the same cwd gets `BUSY <first id>` exit 3 while the first runs, and succeeds after the first finishes AND after the first supervisor is SIGKILLed; read-only runs never BUSY; watch reports a SIGKILLed supervisor's RUNNING record as ERROR \"supervisor died\".\nHygiene (learned in #7): fake agents block on a release file (`while [ ! -e \"$REL\" ]; do sleep 0.05; done`), never fixed sleeps, for any RUNNING-state assertion. Idle windows in tests are tiny (env/flags) and every wait has a hard upper bound so a bug fails instead of hanging.\n\nGates: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test` all pass. Commit message conventional, ending `Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@cursor.com>`.\n\n## Completion bar\nReport the commit SHA and the test summary line, or a failure triage — nothing in between. Then **Friction**: up to 3 bullets on what slowed you, what this brief got wrong or left out, what you'd change (\"none\" is fine). End with a STATUS line.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"b6dfbf0d-2164-45e3-a9e5-f79f7585081e"}
