{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`abee2ce464480ef624091724e6371bc2af28a221`\n\n`cargo test`: 241 unit, 16 cli_e2e, 3 e2e passed; 1 live ignored.\n\n**Friction:**\n- `FinalizeCtx` lives in `src/types.rs`, which the file fence did not list. The gate timeout field had to go there.\n- The sample record uses short `hash subject` commits and `lastHeartbeatAt` on a finished job. The serializer stores full `git rev-list` hashes and drops `lastHeartbeatAt` once the job is terminal.\n- The inherited lock fd has to get `FD_CLOEXEC` inside the supervisor. Otherwise the agent keeps the flock after `SIGKILL` and the next writer stays `BUSY`.\n\nSTATUS: DONE"}]},"session_id":"b6dfbf0d-2164-45e3-a9e5-f79f7585081e"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":1281509,"duration_api_ms":1281509,"is_error":false,"result":"I'll implement issue #9 on this branch: gate wiring, change-set, idle watchdog, and the cross-process write lock. First I'll read the issue rulings, the spec, and the files the brief names.Issue #9 is wiring plus a file lock. Next I’ll read the CLI, status record, finalize, gate, and git code so the new pieces match what already exists.The supervisor already runs the gate, change-set, and idle watchdog. I’ll wire the CLI flags and record fields, then add the flock and the dead-supervisor check.The gate timeout now rides on the finalize context. Next I’ll wire `run`, the supervisor, and `watch` to the lock and the new flags.Tests and clippy are clean. I’ll commit on this branch and leave it unpushed.`abee2ce464480ef624091724e6371bc2af28a221`\n\n`cargo test`: 241 unit, 16 cli_e2e, 3 e2e passed; 1 live ignored.\n\n**Friction:**\n- `FinalizeCtx` lives in `src/types.rs`, which the file fence did not list. The gate timeout field had to go there.\n- The sample record uses short `hash subject` commits and `lastHeartbeatAt` on a finished job. The serializer stores full `git rev-list` hashes and drops `lastHeartbeatAt` once the job is terminal.\n- The inherited lock fd has to get `FD_CLOEXEC` inside the supervisor. Otherwise the agent keeps the flock after `SIGKILL` and the next writer stays `BUSY`.\n\nSTATUS: DONE","session_id":"b6dfbf0d-2164-45e3-a9e5-f79f7585081e","request_id":"cf64fe77-700f-4a00-9174-0ecdd691d677","usage":{"inputTokens":224860,"outputTokens":85191,"cacheReadTokens":3536256,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
